STEP 2 — Python virtual environment (venv)

What I did:
- Created a virtual environment inside the backend folder:
    backend/venv/
- Upgraded pip inside it to the latest version.

How to use it later (Windows):
- Activate:   backend\venv\Scripts\activate
- Or call Python directly without activating:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe <script.py>

Verified:
- Python version: 3.13.2
- pip version:    26.2.1

Why:
- A venv keeps this project's Python packages separate from the rest of the
  computer, so versions never clash with other projects.
